Since the bases are parallel, the interior angles at $W$ and $V$ must sum to $180^\circ$.  Since we know the angles at $W$ and $V$, we can find angle angle at $W$.  The two interior angles of triangle $WVX$ must add up to the angle at $W$ in the trapezoid.  Using the formula for the sum of the interior angles of a triangle we have $\angle W + 30^\circ + 75^\circ = 180^\circ$, so $\angle W = 75^\circ$.

